10
01:00:37,500 --> 01:00:43,500
Direct action is a form of activism in which participants use
economic power or political power to achieve their goals.

11
01:06:41,250 --> 01:06:47,250
The aim of direct action is to either obstruct a certain practice such as a government's laws or
actions or to draw attention to and create a dialogue in order to solve perceived problems.

12
01:12:45,000 --> 01:12:51,000
Direct action may include activities, that can be either violent or nonviolent, targeting people,
groups, institutions, actions, or property that its participants deem objectionable.

13
01:18:48,750 --> 01:18:54,750
Violent direct action may include political violence,
assault, arson, sabotage, and property destruction.

14
01:24:52,500 --> 01:24:58,500
Nonviolent direct action may include peaceful demonstrations, civil
disobedience, sit-ins, strikes, and counter-economics.

15
01:30:56,250 --> 01:31:02,250
The tone is intense.
